coverage:
The paper is about 12.7k lines of LaTeX in 11 sections. I read these in full and checked them line by line:
- 00 (introduction).
- 01 (framework): uniform-bound, extraction, closure, pullback, capacity, restriction and information lemmas, including the chain-rule step in Lemma fw-information.
- 08 (round-cone exponent):
  - the jitter averaging and the r^2/r^{-3} test-volume split in Prop rt-planck;
  - plane-slab estimates (tiny-cap and the sec bound): I checked the Lorentz change (L) symbolically, including preservation of ty-|b|^2 and |A'|^2=|A|^2/D_A, plus the W=Delta^8 and Delta^{-eta/2} tile arithmetic and the GWZ-to-L^3 step;
  - rarity transfer: the q^{2/3} bound via Holder;
  - profiles: excess definition and Lipschitz branching counts;
  - classical angular memory: m=3-p=2-2d+2Gamma;
  - interval-density (Vitali argument) and dyadic stationarity;
  - width derivative (rv);
  - the outgoing entropy proof (round-out): 4-pin Gram-Schmidt reveal, data-processing bound for the pin information, Ramsey or two-direction secant argument, projected incidence giving d+min(1,d+m/2);
  - the final descent Lemma rt-descent and the algebra of both cases: E_t=1+3d-2Gamma-o_T, E_v<=m+o_T-d-3, giving -2Gamma in each branch, and the classical D(1,0) contradiction.
- 09 (physical half-wave):
  - change to null coordinates and its Jacobian;
  - Bernstein and small-energy case;
  - kernel localization;
  - predecessor-volume lemma: I verified in sympy the discriminant identity |F_x+2VF_w|^2=1+4(beta+ku)G-4kF, that G is constant along rays, that F is affine on rays, the input-plane equation, the slice Jacobian r^4/(1+|A*|^2) and the restricted-gradient formula;
  - weight floor r^4 f^{1-eta}>=H^2;
  - synthesis lemma exponents;
  - level-set or dyadic-amplitude summation;
  - frequency summation;
  - interpolation exponents for the full range;
  - maximal corollary exponent s>1-2/p.
- 10 (Bochner-Riesz): multiplier factorization and maximal-function domination, nonmaximal interpolation and duality, and K^delta decay at the p=1 endpoint.

From section 03 I read the GWZ statement and its Hilbert-valued extension, the kinetic lemma statement, LP, and the conditional incidence bootstrap. For the bootstrap I checked that the fixed point (2a+g, a+2g) or (1+a, 1+g) solves the Ren-Wang min equations.

From section 02 I read the cylinder model, tests, localization, polynomial reduction, one-time bound (checked ell^{1+eta/2}, p>=1 and the Gamma=d+(1-p)/2 identity) and peeling. From section 07 I read the round model, regularity, packet locality and covering.

I did not read these in detail, beyond spot checks: the rest of 02, most of 03 (the Ren-Wang adaptation and the cylinder zero-cost exclusions), and all of 04 (canonical names), 05 (interior inequalities), 06 (cylinder actions) and the rest of 07 (thin-shape transfer and the free-composition proposition). Together that is roughly 8-9k lines, and it carries the proof of the cylinder Theorem, which Theorem round needs. My no_gap_found verdict is therefore limited to the endgame and the reductions; it is not a certification of the cylinder machinery.
